INSERT INTO sat_questions (question_id, external_id, vault_id, disclosed_item_id, source, program, test_type, test_type_desc, domain, primary_class_cd, skill_cd, skill_desc, difficulty, score_band_range_cd, question_type, stimulus_html, stem_html, answer_options, correct_answer, answer_keys, rationale_html, correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale, image_count, parent_template_name, parent_template_id, template_cluster_id, template_cluster_name, origin, position, answer_style, section, raw_payload, created_date, updated_date) VALUES
    ($SATQ$622a351d$SATQ$, $SATQ$57bc16b7-b31e-43cd-9f03-a9aea8afed33$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$3347dee1-207b-4621-851e-66593c19aefd$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>In 1978, S&aacute;mi activists staged protests to block the construction of a dam on the Alta River in Norway.</li>
<li>The dam would disrupt S&aacute;mi fishing and reindeer herding.</li>
<li>The dam was ultimately built, but the Alta conflict had a lasting impact.</li>
<li>It brought international attention to the issue of S&aacute;mi rights.</li>
<li>It led to a set of 2005 legal protections establishing S&aacute;mi rights to lands, waters, and resources.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to make and support a generalization about the Alta conflict. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"11904451-b17f-4b9b-80e2-89719e2b1226","content":"<p>During the Alta conflict, S&aacute;mi activists staged protests to block the construction of a dam on the Alta River in Norway that would disrupt local fishing and reindeer herding.</p>"},{"id":"258ff4fb-ab9d-4107-9758-af426ea80c25","content":"<p>Although the dam that the S&aacute;mi activists had protested was ultimately built, the Alta conflict had a lasting impact.</p>"},{"id":"aab63ebc-0542-4da5-87de-21d1887fc902","content":"<p>S&aacute;mi rights to lands, waters, and resources received international attention and legal protections as a result of the Alta conflict.</p>"},{"id":"4c2d84fb-a280-4f20-8c9e-2db5461d881e","content":"<p>The Alta conflict had a lasting impact, resulting in international attention and legal protections for S&aacute;mi rights to lands, waters, and resources.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["4c2d84fb-a280-4f20-8c9e-2db5461d881e"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. It makes a generalization&mdash;the conflict had a lasting impact&mdash;and then supports it with evidence&mdash;the attention and protections were results of the conflict. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t make a generalization about the conflict. It describes a specific event from the conflict. Choice B is incorrect. This choice makes a generalization about the Alta conflict, but doesn&rsquo;t support it. Choice C is incorrect. This choice makes a statement about the aftermath of the conflict, but doesn&rsquo;t support it. The statement is also a little too specific to be a generalization. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-SYN-H002$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$62ac0f2f-fca6-4427-9851-7f4c3be434dd$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"622a351d","external_id":"57bc16b7-b31e-43cd-9f03-a9aea8afed33","vaultid":"3347dee1-207b-4621-851e-66593c19aefd","uId":"a1573034-5d1d-40c4-8130-7f64e3198c83","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>In 1978, S&aacute;mi activists staged protests to block the construction of a dam on the Alta River in Norway.</li>\n<li>The dam would disrupt S&aacute;mi fishing and reindeer herding.</li>\n<li>The dam was ultimately built, but the Alta conflict had a lasting impact.</li>\n<li>It brought international attention to the issue of S&aacute;mi rights.</li>\n<li>It led to a set of 2005 legal protections establishing S&aacute;mi rights to lands, waters, and resources.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to make and support a generalization about the Alta conflict. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"11904451-b17f-4b9b-80e2-89719e2b1226","content":"<p>During the Alta conflict, S&aacute;mi activists staged protests to block the construction of a dam on the Alta River in Norway that would disrupt local fishing and reindeer herding.</p>"},{"id":"258ff4fb-ab9d-4107-9758-af426ea80c25","content":"<p>Although the dam that the S&aacute;mi activists had protested was ultimately built, the Alta conflict had a lasting impact.</p>"},{"id":"aab63ebc-0542-4da5-87de-21d1887fc902","content":"<p>S&aacute;mi rights to lands, waters, and resources received international attention and legal protections as a result of the Alta conflict.</p>"},{"id":"4c2d84fb-a280-4f20-8c9e-2db5461d881e","content":"<p>The Alta conflict had a lasting impact, resulting in international attention and legal protections for S&aacute;mi rights to lands, waters, and resources.</p>"}],"keys":["4c2d84fb-a280-4f20-8c9e-2db5461d881e"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. It makes a generalization&mdash;the conflict had a lasting impact&mdash;and then supports it with evidence&mdash;the attention and protections were results of the conflict. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t make a generalization about the conflict. It describes a specific event from the conflict. Choice B is incorrect. This choice makes a generalization about the Alta conflict, but doesn&rsquo;t support it. Choice C is incorrect. This choice makes a statement about the aftermath of the conflict, but doesn&rsquo;t support it. The statement is also a little too specific to be a generalization. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-SYN-H002","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"62ac0f2f-fca6-4427-9851-7f4c3be434dd","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959372,"updateDate":1691007959372}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959372, 1691007959372),
    ($SATQ$6249b173$SATQ$, $SATQ$79bc06dd-c018-47ad-b4a1-8672599b0cdf$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$a4ed1e61-4733-46e4-89dc-67d2f527f4d9$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>In 2018 researchers Adwait Deshpande, Shreejata Gupta, and Anindya Sinha were observing wild macaques in India&rsquo;s Bandipur National Park.</li>
<li>They saw macaques calling out to and gesturing at humans who were eating or carrying food.</li>
<li>They designed a study to find out if the macaques were intentionally communicating to try to persuade the humans to share their food.</li>
<li>In the study trials, macaques frequently called out to and gestured at humans holding food.</li>
<li>In the study trials, macaques called out to and gestured at empty-handed humans less frequently.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to present the study&rsquo;s results. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"87400934-ccfb-4e5b-8902-e9385f91bafb","content":"<p>Macaques in the study called out to and gestured more frequently at humans holding food than at empty-handed humans.</p>"},{"id":"6d721db5-d819-49b0-98c8-e0f5b0180fb8","content":"<p>In 2018, researchers who had observed macaques in India&rsquo;s Bandipur National Park calling out to and gesturing at humans designed a study.</p>"},{"id":"5716b23b-2922-4bee-9574-645566558996","content":"<p>The researchers hoped to find out if the macaques were intentionally communicating to try to persuade humans to share their food.</p>"},{"id":"12aaa01a-b84a-4119-a522-c92122b09f6d","content":"<p>The researchers studied how macaques behaved around both humans holding food and empty-handed humans.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["87400934-ccfb-4e5b-8902-e9385f91bafb"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. This choice presents the study&rsquo;s results from the last two bullet points. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This choice describes the background and motivation of the study but not the outcome or findings. Choice C is incorrect. This choice describes the research question or hypothesis of the study but not the evidence or conclusion. Choice D is incorrect. This choice describes the method or design of the study but not the actual results. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-SYN-M009$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$294c2172-3b46-43f2-a57d-7347863db336$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"6249b173","external_id":"79bc06dd-c018-47ad-b4a1-8672599b0cdf","vaultid":"a4ed1e61-4733-46e4-89dc-67d2f527f4d9","uId":"2fc06986-7199-4b20-9bf4-6885c467f376","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>In 2018 researchers Adwait Deshpande, Shreejata Gupta, and Anindya Sinha were observing wild macaques in India&rsquo;s Bandipur National Park.</li>\n<li>They saw macaques calling out to and gesturing at humans who were eating or carrying food.</li>\n<li>They designed a study to find out if the macaques were intentionally communicating to try to persuade the humans to share their food.</li>\n<li>In the study trials, macaques frequently called out to and gestured at humans holding food.</li>\n<li>In the study trials, macaques called out to and gestured at empty-handed humans less frequently.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to present the study&rsquo;s results. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"87400934-ccfb-4e5b-8902-e9385f91bafb","content":"<p>Macaques in the study called out to and gestured more frequently at humans holding food than at empty-handed humans.</p>"},{"id":"6d721db5-d819-49b0-98c8-e0f5b0180fb8","content":"<p>In 2018, researchers who had observed macaques in India&rsquo;s Bandipur National Park calling out to and gesturing at humans designed a study.</p>"},{"id":"5716b23b-2922-4bee-9574-645566558996","content":"<p>The researchers hoped to find out if the macaques were intentionally communicating to try to persuade humans to share their food.</p>"},{"id":"12aaa01a-b84a-4119-a522-c92122b09f6d","content":"<p>The researchers studied how macaques behaved around both humans holding food and empty-handed humans.</p>"}],"keys":["87400934-ccfb-4e5b-8902-e9385f91bafb"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. This choice presents the study&rsquo;s results from the last two bullet points. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This choice describes the background and motivation of the study but not the outcome or findings. Choice C is incorrect. This choice describes the research question or hypothesis of the study but not the evidence or conclusion. Choice D is incorrect. This choice describes the method or design of the study but not the actual results. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-SYN-M009","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"294c2172-3b46-43f2-a57d-7347863db336","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959372,"updateDate":1691007959372}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959372, 1691007959372),
    ($SATQ$6351062d$SATQ$, $SATQ$b14bc05c-86a9-4ef5-8226-2f0af8ff86e9$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$94673406-3c03-4d8f-b66d-41e91eafd53d$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>In the late 1890s, over 14,000 unique varieties of apples were grown in the US.</li>
<li>The rise of industrial agriculture in the mid-1900s narrowed the range of commercially grown crops.</li>
<li>Thousands of apple varieties considered less suitable for commercial growth were lost.</li>
<li>Today, only 15 apple varieties dominate the market, making up 90% of apples purchased in the US.</li>
<li>The Lost Apple Project, based in Washington State, attempts to find and grow lost apple varieties.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to emphasize the decline in unique apple varieties in the US and specify why this decline occurred. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish these goals?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"758dbda1-54d2-46de-9782-4d1bceca65d7","content":"<p>The Lost Apple Project is dedicated to finding some of the apple varieties lost following a shift in agricultural practices in the mid-1900s.</p>"},{"id":"ba5fd11a-6dd7-499b-911b-583e3270ef29","content":"<p>While over 14,000 apple varieties were grown in the US in the late 1890s, only 15 unique varieties make up most of the apples sold today.</p>"},{"id":"b0f40a77-d98f-441f-af87-ced28251e574","content":"<p>Since the rise of industrial agriculture, US farmers have mainly grown the same few unique apple varieties, resulting in the loss of thousands of varieties less suitable for commercial growth.</p>"},{"id":"3de2c8c5-a499-4795-8758-8ca7ade70c7d","content":"<p>As industrial agriculture rose to prominence in the mid-1900s, the number of crops selected for cultivation decreased dramatically.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["b0f40a77-d98f-441f-af87-ced28251e574"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes the decline in unique apple varieties in the US and specifies why this decline occurred, noting that thousands of apple varieties were lost because US farmers started mainly growing the same few unique varieties. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence introduces the Lost Apple Project; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize the decline in unique apple varieties in the US and specify why this decline occurred.&nbsp;Choice B is incorrect. While the sentence emphasizes the decline in unique apple varieties in the US, it doesn&rsquo;t explain why this decline occurred. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes the general decline of crop varieties in the mid-1900s; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize the specific decline in unique apple varieties in the US. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-744-SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$78cc11f6-2358-4985-9ca9-66626f00e528$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"6351062d","external_id":"b14bc05c-86a9-4ef5-8226-2f0af8ff86e9","vaultid":"94673406-3c03-4d8f-b66d-41e91eafd53d","uId":"e4dcb98e-2c0b-4e6a-82f6-cb9ec71df3e5","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>In the late 1890s, over 14,000 unique varieties of apples were grown in the US.</li>\n<li>The rise of industrial agriculture in the mid-1900s narrowed the range of commercially grown crops.</li>\n<li>Thousands of apple varieties considered less suitable for commercial growth were lost.</li>\n<li>Today, only 15 apple varieties dominate the market, making up 90% of apples purchased in the US.</li>\n<li>The Lost Apple Project, based in Washington State, attempts to find and grow lost apple varieties.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to emphasize the decline in unique apple varieties in the US and specify why this decline occurred. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish these goals?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"758dbda1-54d2-46de-9782-4d1bceca65d7","content":"<p>The Lost Apple Project is dedicated to finding some of the apple varieties lost following a shift in agricultural practices in the mid-1900s.</p>"},{"id":"ba5fd11a-6dd7-499b-911b-583e3270ef29","content":"<p>While over 14,000 apple varieties were grown in the US in the late 1890s, only 15 unique varieties make up most of the apples sold today.</p>"},{"id":"b0f40a77-d98f-441f-af87-ced28251e574","content":"<p>Since the rise of industrial agriculture, US farmers have mainly grown the same few unique apple varieties, resulting in the loss of thousands of varieties less suitable for commercial growth.</p>"},{"id":"3de2c8c5-a499-4795-8758-8ca7ade70c7d","content":"<p>As industrial agriculture rose to prominence in the mid-1900s, the number of crops selected for cultivation decreased dramatically.</p>"}],"keys":["b0f40a77-d98f-441f-af87-ced28251e574"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes the decline in unique apple varieties in the US and specifies why this decline occurred, noting that thousands of apple varieties were lost because US farmers started mainly growing the same few unique varieties. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence introduces the Lost Apple Project; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize the decline in unique apple varieties in the US and specify why this decline occurred.&nbsp;Choice B is incorrect. While the sentence emphasizes the decline in unique apple varieties in the US, it doesn&rsquo;t explain why this decline occurred. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes the general decline of crop varieties in the mid-1900s; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize the specific decline in unique apple varieties in the US. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-744-SYN","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"78cc11f6-2358-4985-9ca9-66626f00e528","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959350,"updateDate":1691007959350}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959350, 1691007959350),
    ($SATQ$63a4fa29$SATQ$, $SATQ$f068fffb-1cc7-440d-abce-4ab05d1fcf20$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$ed189b54-9100-4626-9da8-d9208b04a967$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>In 2013, archaeologists studied cat bone fragments they had found in the ruins of Quanhucun, a Chinese farming village.</li>
<li>The fragments were estimated to be 5,300 years old.</li>
<li>A chemical analysis of the fragments revealed that the cats had consumed large amounts of grain.</li>
<li>The grain consumption is evidence that the Quanhucun cats may have been domesticated.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to present the Quanhucun study and its conclusions. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"397b4710-3f06-45db-91bf-626ffc350ca9","content":"<p>As part of a 2013 study of cat domestication, a chemical analysis was conducted on cat bone fragments found in Quanhucun, China.</p>"},{"id":"5c807366-1c09-4c78-bc37-14b425fb433a","content":"<p>A 2013 analysis of cat bone fragments found in Quanhucun, China, suggests that cats there may have been domesticated 5,300 years ago.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"6f5627d3-eb5c-4633-a7a7-c077ea797dc2","content":"<p>In 2013, archaeologists studied what cats in Quanhucun, China, had eaten more than 5,000 years ago.</p>"},{"id":"9d6c66a8-7f52-4dd5-a0b2-c7ce4b68dae1","content":"<p>Cat bone fragments estimated to be 5,300 years old were found in Quanhucun, China, in 2013.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["5c807366-1c09-4c78-bc37-14b425fb433a"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. The sentence presents the study, describing it as a 2013 analysis of Quanhucun cat bone fragments, and its conclusions, indicating what the analysis suggests about cat domestication in Quanhucun.&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the sentence focuses on the study&rsquo;s methodology; it doesn&rsquo;t present conclusions from the study. Choice C is incorrect. While the sentence provides a general overview of the study, it doesn&rsquo;t present conclusions from the study. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence describes a finding from the study; it doesn&rsquo;t present conclusions from the study. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-752-SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$e885d79c-f796-4540-b4e6-7f4b7c6a7757$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"63a4fa29","external_id":"f068fffb-1cc7-440d-abce-4ab05d1fcf20","vaultid":"ed189b54-9100-4626-9da8-d9208b04a967","uId":"331aaafc-3945-41e8-acd0-2acf44adaa23","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>In 2013, archaeologists studied cat bone fragments they had found in the ruins of Quanhucun, a Chinese farming village.</li>\n<li>The fragments were estimated to be 5,300 years old.</li>\n<li>A chemical analysis of the fragments revealed that the cats had consumed large amounts of grain.</li>\n<li>The grain consumption is evidence that the Quanhucun cats may have been domesticated.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to present the Quanhucun study and its conclusions. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"397b4710-3f06-45db-91bf-626ffc350ca9","content":"<p>As part of a 2013 study of cat domestication, a chemical analysis was conducted on cat bone fragments found in Quanhucun, China.</p>"},{"id":"5c807366-1c09-4c78-bc37-14b425fb433a","content":"<p>A 2013 analysis of cat bone fragments found in Quanhucun, China, suggests that cats there may have been domesticated 5,300 years ago.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"6f5627d3-eb5c-4633-a7a7-c077ea797dc2","content":"<p>In 2013, archaeologists studied what cats in Quanhucun, China, had eaten more than 5,000 years ago.</p>"},{"id":"9d6c66a8-7f52-4dd5-a0b2-c7ce4b68dae1","content":"<p>Cat bone fragments estimated to be 5,300 years old were found in Quanhucun, China, in 2013.</p>"}],"keys":["5c807366-1c09-4c78-bc37-14b425fb433a"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. The sentence presents the study, describing it as a 2013 analysis of Quanhucun cat bone fragments, and its conclusions, indicating what the analysis suggests about cat domestication in Quanhucun.&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the sentence focuses on the study&rsquo;s methodology; it doesn&rsquo;t present conclusions from the study. Choice C is incorrect. While the sentence provides a general overview of the study, it doesn&rsquo;t present conclusions from the study. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence describes a finding from the study; it doesn&rsquo;t present conclusions from the study. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-752-SYN","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"e885d79c-f796-4540-b4e6-7f4b7c6a7757","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959350,"updateDate":1691007959350}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959350, 1691007959350),
    ($SATQ$63c73b50$SATQ$, $SATQ$45aaead0-9d12-46cb-bfc0-daf21dbeaeb5$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$4fa7f29e-8876-45ad-aae9-9ac3f9e72ba3$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>In 2018, Kurt Luther and Vikram Mohanty created the web-based tool Civil War Photo Sleuth (CWPS). A user uploading an unknown Civil War soldier&rsquo;s photograph to CWPS first tags the photo with all known information. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> CWPS&rsquo;s facial-recognition software analyzes twenty-seven different physical features and looks for matches to tagged images already in the database.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"8e7718bd-d74c-41d4-9346-8430cabd5a83","content":"<p>Then,&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"805ca27a-70fc-4f91-9715-a6a4840abaec","content":"<p>In fact,</p>"},{"id":"b04cb553-8707-4920-8e62-822110967a12","content":"<p>Likewise,</p>"},{"id":"9162031e-e747-4809-826d-2b22cd7af91f","content":"<p>For example,&nbsp;</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["8e7718bd-d74c-41d4-9346-8430cabd5a83"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. &ldquo;Then&rdquo; indicates that the events in this sentence took place after the events in the previous sentence. Only after users upload images of unknown soldiers can those images be analyzed. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This transition is used to emphasize the truth of a statement that modifies the previous statement. But this sentence doesn&rsquo;t modify the step described in the previous statement: instead, it introduces an entirely new step in the process. So &ldquo;in fact&rdquo; wouldn&rsquo;t make sense here. Choice C is incorrect. This choice uses a transition that indicates the addition of a new but related idea, which doesn&rsquo;t make sense here. Analyzing the physical features in the uploaded photographs isn&rsquo;t a similar idea, but rather the next step in the process. Choice D is incorrect. This choice uses an exemplification transition, which doesn&rsquo;t make sense here. Analyzing physical features is not an example of uploading and tagging an image. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-TRA-M007$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$367201eb-bbd5-44ef-977e-f7296e17c447$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"63c73b50","external_id":"45aaead0-9d12-46cb-bfc0-daf21dbeaeb5","vaultid":"4fa7f29e-8876-45ad-aae9-9ac3f9e72ba3","uId":"b7f7bddc-4045-4249-a196-ce5ad3792f3b","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>In 2018, Kurt Luther and Vikram Mohanty created the web-based tool Civil War Photo Sleuth (CWPS). A user uploading an unknown Civil War soldier&rsquo;s photograph to CWPS first tags the photo with all known information. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> CWPS&rsquo;s facial-recognition software analyzes twenty-seven different physical features and looks for matches to tagged images already in the database.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"8e7718bd-d74c-41d4-9346-8430cabd5a83","content":"<p>Then,&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"805ca27a-70fc-4f91-9715-a6a4840abaec","content":"<p>In fact,</p>"},{"id":"b04cb553-8707-4920-8e62-822110967a12","content":"<p>Likewise,</p>"},{"id":"9162031e-e747-4809-826d-2b22cd7af91f","content":"<p>For example,&nbsp;</p>"}],"keys":["8e7718bd-d74c-41d4-9346-8430cabd5a83"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. &ldquo;Then&rdquo; indicates that the events in this sentence took place after the events in the previous sentence. Only after users upload images of unknown soldiers can those images be analyzed. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This transition is used to emphasize the truth of a statement that modifies the previous statement. But this sentence doesn&rsquo;t modify the step described in the previous statement: instead, it introduces an entirely new step in the process. So &ldquo;in fact&rdquo; wouldn&rsquo;t make sense here. Choice C is incorrect. This choice uses a transition that indicates the addition of a new but related idea, which doesn&rsquo;t make sense here. Analyzing the physical features in the uploaded photographs isn&rsquo;t a similar idea, but rather the next step in the process. Choice D is incorrect. This choice uses an exemplification transition, which doesn&rsquo;t make sense here. Analyzing physical features is not an example of uploading and tagging an image. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-TRA-M007","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"367201eb-bbd5-44ef-977e-f7296e17c447","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959374,"updateDate":1691007959374}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959374, 1691007959374),
    ($SATQ$64e88c58$SATQ$, $SATQ$ca621cb1-642b-480b-b511-a086f4c7f525$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$78881397-2e3d-4689-9661-22b3dbf7258c$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>In 1971, experimental musician Pauline Oliveros created <em>Sonic Meditations</em>.</li>
<li><em>Sonic Meditations</em> is not music but rather a series of sound-based exercises called meditations.</li>
<li>Each meditation consists of instructions for participants to make, imagine, listen to, or remember sounds.</li>
<li>The instructions for Meditation V state, &ldquo;walk so silently that the bottoms of your feet become ears.&rdquo;</li>
<li>Those for Meditation XVIII state, &ldquo;listen to a sound until you no longer recognize it.&rdquo;</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to provide an explanation and an example of Oliveros&rsquo;s <em>Sonic Meditations</em>. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a4cedc4f-c1ba-4035-b810-01895775219f","content":"<p><em>Sonic Meditations</em> is not music but rather a series of sound-based meditations that consist of instructions; Meditation XVIII, for instance, instructs participants to &ldquo;listen to a sound until you no longer recognize it.&rdquo;</p>"},{"id":"eeb9df68-273d-49d6-9957-3520e1e1145f","content":"<p>In 1971, Oliveros created <em>Sonic Meditations</em>, a series of meditations that consist of instructions for participants to make, imagine, listen to, or remember sounds.</p>"},{"id":"73772020-490f-4c2d-b797-a5c54cbe3c7b","content":"<p>&ldquo;Walk so silently that the bottoms of your feet become ears&rdquo; is one example of the instructions found in Oliveros&rsquo;s <em>Sonic Meditations</em>.</p>"},{"id":"544ee6b9-c1f8-4098-8c2a-3c9f8c9319ca","content":"<p>While both meditations consist of instructions, Meditation XVIII instructs participants to &ldquo;listen,&rdquo; whereas Meditation V instructs participants to &ldquo;walk.&rdquo;</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["a4cedc4f-c1ba-4035-b810-01895775219f"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. It describes what a &ldquo;Sonic Meditation&rdquo; is, and then gives an example in the form of Meditation XVIII. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This choice describes what a &ldquo;Sonic Meditation&rdquo; is, but doesn&rsquo;t give an example of one. Choice C is incorrect. This choice gives an example of a &ldquo;Sonic Meditation,&rdquo; but doesn&rsquo;t explain what the meditations are. Choice D is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t describe what a &ldquo;Sonic Meditation&rdquo; is. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-SYN-H003$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$7b9fa497-7cb4-47a3-b7a5-3ead9745d4aa$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"64e88c58","external_id":"ca621cb1-642b-480b-b511-a086f4c7f525","vaultid":"78881397-2e3d-4689-9661-22b3dbf7258c","uId":"4a0d8a1d-f650-45ac-b5fe-a7e13723fd4c","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>In 1971, experimental musician Pauline Oliveros created <em>Sonic Meditations</em>.</li>\n<li><em>Sonic Meditations</em> is not music but rather a series of sound-based exercises called meditations.</li>\n<li>Each meditation consists of instructions for participants to make, imagine, listen to, or remember sounds.</li>\n<li>The instructions for Meditation V state, &ldquo;walk so silently that the bottoms of your feet become ears.&rdquo;</li>\n<li>Those for Meditation XVIII state, &ldquo;listen to a sound until you no longer recognize it.&rdquo;</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to provide an explanation and an example of Oliveros&rsquo;s <em>Sonic Meditations</em>. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"a4cedc4f-c1ba-4035-b810-01895775219f","content":"<p><em>Sonic Meditations</em> is not music but rather a series of sound-based meditations that consist of instructions; Meditation XVIII, for instance, instructs participants to &ldquo;listen to a sound until you no longer recognize it.&rdquo;</p>"},{"id":"eeb9df68-273d-49d6-9957-3520e1e1145f","content":"<p>In 1971, Oliveros created <em>Sonic Meditations</em>, a series of meditations that consist of instructions for participants to make, imagine, listen to, or remember sounds.</p>"},{"id":"73772020-490f-4c2d-b797-a5c54cbe3c7b","content":"<p>&ldquo;Walk so silently that the bottoms of your feet become ears&rdquo; is one example of the instructions found in Oliveros&rsquo;s <em>Sonic Meditations</em>.</p>"},{"id":"544ee6b9-c1f8-4098-8c2a-3c9f8c9319ca","content":"<p>While both meditations consist of instructions, Meditation XVIII instructs participants to &ldquo;listen,&rdquo; whereas Meditation V instructs participants to &ldquo;walk.&rdquo;</p>"}],"keys":["a4cedc4f-c1ba-4035-b810-01895775219f"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. It describes what a &ldquo;Sonic Meditation&rdquo; is, and then gives an example in the form of Meditation XVIII. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This choice describes what a &ldquo;Sonic Meditation&rdquo; is, but doesn&rsquo;t give an example of one. Choice C is incorrect. This choice gives an example of a &ldquo;Sonic Meditation,&rdquo; but doesn&rsquo;t explain what the meditations are. Choice D is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t describe what a &ldquo;Sonic Meditation&rdquo; is. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-SYN-H003","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"7b9fa497-7cb4-47a3-b7a5-3ead9745d4aa","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959372,"updateDate":1691007959372}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959372, 1691007959372),
    ($SATQ$660d50dc$SATQ$, $SATQ$6dbea806-7237-4202-a6ed-d4ab201a9cef$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$a20dbde7-c598-492b-ad5c-956ea7fee863$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Samuel Coleridge-Taylor was a prominent classical music composer from England who toured the US three times in the early 1900s. The child of a West African father and an English mother, Coleridge-Taylor emphasized his mixed-race ancestry. For example, he referred to himself as Anglo-African. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> he incorporated the sounds of traditional African music into his classical music compositions.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"6f35c026-dfa1-4431-b2e7-e65a9dcb70e7","content":"<p>In addition,</p>"},{"id":"55202922-2415-491a-9d49-90e391218e07","content":"<p>Actually,</p>"},{"id":"cbca548e-5f83-47e1-be2c-d58b5b4fc4e5","content":"<p>However,</p>"},{"id":"7d81d462-1c78-45c5-a7f5-d54f9ba4a0ed","content":"<p>Regardless,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["6f35c026-dfa1-4431-b2e7-e65a9dcb70e7"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. &ldquo;In addition&rdquo; logically signals that the detail in this sentence&mdash;that Coleridge-Taylor included traditional African music in his classical compositions&mdash;adds to the information in the previous sentence. Specifically, the previous sentence indicates one way in which Coleridge-Taylor emphasized his mixed-race ancestry, and the claim that follows indicates a second, additional way. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;actually&rdquo; illogically signals that the detail in this sentence is surprising in light of the information in the previous sentence. Instead, the detail adds to the information, indicating a second, additional way in which Coleridge-Taylor emphasized his mixed-race ancestry. Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;however&rdquo; illogically signals that the detail in this sentence contrasts with the information in the previous sentence. Instead, the detail adds to the information, indicating a second, additional way in which Coleridge-Taylor emphasized his mixed-race ancestry. Choice D is incorrect because &ldquo;regardless&rdquo; illogically signals that the detail in this sentence is true despite the information in the previous sentence. Instead, the detail adds to the information, indicating a second, additional way in which Coleridge-Taylor emphasized his mixed-race ancestry. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-238-TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$72b68781-4d7b-43c1-8f7f-507d3473736a$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"660d50dc","external_id":"6dbea806-7237-4202-a6ed-d4ab201a9cef","vaultid":"a20dbde7-c598-492b-ad5c-956ea7fee863","uId":"033c2e57-8b80-4a8f-a06e-abee4b3a3099","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Samuel Coleridge-Taylor was a prominent classical music composer from England who toured the US three times in the early 1900s. The child of a West African father and an English mother, Coleridge-Taylor emphasized his mixed-race ancestry. For example, he referred to himself as Anglo-African. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> he incorporated the sounds of traditional African music into his classical music compositions.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"6f35c026-dfa1-4431-b2e7-e65a9dcb70e7","content":"<p>In addition,</p>"},{"id":"55202922-2415-491a-9d49-90e391218e07","content":"<p>Actually,</p>"},{"id":"cbca548e-5f83-47e1-be2c-d58b5b4fc4e5","content":"<p>However,</p>"},{"id":"7d81d462-1c78-45c5-a7f5-d54f9ba4a0ed","content":"<p>Regardless,</p>"}],"keys":["6f35c026-dfa1-4431-b2e7-e65a9dcb70e7"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. &ldquo;In addition&rdquo; logically signals that the detail in this sentence&mdash;that Coleridge-Taylor included traditional African music in his classical compositions&mdash;adds to the information in the previous sentence. Specifically, the previous sentence indicates one way in which Coleridge-Taylor emphasized his mixed-race ancestry, and the claim that follows indicates a second, additional way. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;actually&rdquo; illogically signals that the detail in this sentence is surprising in light of the information in the previous sentence. Instead, the detail adds to the information, indicating a second, additional way in which Coleridge-Taylor emphasized his mixed-race ancestry. Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;however&rdquo; illogically signals that the detail in this sentence contrasts with the information in the previous sentence. Instead, the detail adds to the information, indicating a second, additional way in which Coleridge-Taylor emphasized his mixed-race ancestry. Choice D is incorrect because &ldquo;regardless&rdquo; illogically signals that the detail in this sentence is true despite the information in the previous sentence. Instead, the detail adds to the information, indicating a second, additional way in which Coleridge-Taylor emphasized his mixed-race ancestry. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-238-TRA","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"72b68781-4d7b-43c1-8f7f-507d3473736a","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959333,"updateDate":1691007959333}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959333, 1691007959333),
    ($SATQ$6916c8e5$SATQ$, $SATQ$5dc54953-7e21-4e5e-b76a-af27eca7a27a$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$46fe1058-bce8-41a6-b020-f525497158a8$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Laetitia Ky&rsquo;s hair is her art. Inspired by hairstyles from various African tribes, the Ivorian artist uses wire and thread to sculpt her hair into all kinds of shapes. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> she once made her hair into the shape of the continent of Africa&mdash;including the island of Madagascar!</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"6e2892e2-1125-4077-b7ab-5718fa52f52e","content":"<p>Soon,</p>"},{"id":"41c2b20a-1357-4ce8-a99d-b44bb135383c","content":"<p>Elsewhere,</p>"},{"id":"1a382b2d-1479-4863-8357-2a27cd121a64","content":"<p>For example,</p>"},{"id":"e50660dd-3c8c-45da-ba36-85c346a7830c","content":"<p>However,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["1a382b2d-1479-4863-8357-2a27cd121a64"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer. &ldquo;For example&rdquo; logically signals that the following information about Ky&mdash;that she once shaped her hair to look like Africa&mdash;is an example supporting the previous statement that she makes different shapes with her hair. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;soon&rdquo; illogically signals that the event described in this sentence occurred soon after the statement about Ky making different shapes with her hair. Instead, the sentence provides an example of one of these shapes. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;elsewhere&rdquo; illogically signals that the event described in this sentence occurred in a different place than the statement about Ky making different shapes with her hair. Instead, the sentence provides an example of one of these shapes. Choice D is incorrect because &ldquo;however&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence contrasts with the statement that Ky makes different shapes with her hair. Instead, the sentence provides an example of one of these shapes. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-258-TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$cd9086ea-9343-4f16-9bfd-630fec03f4be$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"6916c8e5","external_id":"5dc54953-7e21-4e5e-b76a-af27eca7a27a","vaultid":"46fe1058-bce8-41a6-b020-f525497158a8","uId":"f6b16091-9e6d-4800-9abb-b049ba64aa2d","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Laetitia Ky&rsquo;s hair is her art. Inspired by hairstyles from various African tribes, the Ivorian artist uses wire and thread to sculpt her hair into all kinds of shapes. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> she once made her hair into the shape of the continent of Africa&mdash;including the island of Madagascar!</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"6e2892e2-1125-4077-b7ab-5718fa52f52e","content":"<p>Soon,</p>"},{"id":"41c2b20a-1357-4ce8-a99d-b44bb135383c","content":"<p>Elsewhere,</p>"},{"id":"1a382b2d-1479-4863-8357-2a27cd121a64","content":"<p>For example,</p>"},{"id":"e50660dd-3c8c-45da-ba36-85c346a7830c","content":"<p>However,</p>"}],"keys":["1a382b2d-1479-4863-8357-2a27cd121a64"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer. &ldquo;For example&rdquo; logically signals that the following information about Ky&mdash;that she once shaped her hair to look like Africa&mdash;is an example supporting the previous statement that she makes different shapes with her hair. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;soon&rdquo; illogically signals that the event described in this sentence occurred soon after the statement about Ky making different shapes with her hair. Instead, the sentence provides an example of one of these shapes. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;elsewhere&rdquo; illogically signals that the event described in this sentence occurred in a different place than the statement about Ky making different shapes with her hair. Instead, the sentence provides an example of one of these shapes. Choice D is incorrect because &ldquo;however&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence contrasts with the statement that Ky makes different shapes with her hair. Instead, the sentence provides an example of one of these shapes. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-258-TRA","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"cd9086ea-9343-4f16-9bfd-630fec03f4be","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959334,"updateDate":1691007959334}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959334, 1691007959334),
    ($SATQ$6a5939c2$SATQ$, $SATQ$d72a5a0b-bdd4-477d-a9f4-008853b581b1$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Paleontologists once thought that early apes lived in tropical forests, but recent research suggests that they may have actually lived in savannas. Tropical forests are humid and have many trees spaced close together. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> savannas are drier, and their trees are spaced further apart.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"1c278495-fe98-443e-a712-9481cc94754f","content":"<p>For instance,</p>"},{"id":"605c1f47-0ed2-491b-8c60-5b722b237271","content":"<p>In comparison,</p>"},{"id":"31ab7665-d5ca-44f9-a0fc-4e64eb3489e7","content":"<p>Firstly,</p>"},{"id":"3c981bbf-3c52-4d2e-add6-3e38a3bdb723","content":"<p>In conclusion,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["605c1f47-0ed2-491b-8c60-5b722b237271"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. "In comparison" logically signals that the description of savannas in this sentence&mdash;that they are drier and their trees are spaced further apart&mdash;forms a comparison with the description of tropical forests in the previous sentence.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because "for instance" illogically signals that the description of savannas in this sentence exemplifies the description of tropical forests in the previous sentence. Instead, this description forms a comparison with the description of tropical forests. Choice C is incorrect because "firstly" illogically signals that the description of savannas in this sentence indicates the first in a series of things. Instead, this description forms a comparison with the description of tropical forests in the previous sentence. Choice D is incorrect because "in conclusion" illogically signals that the description of savannas in this sentence concludes or summarizes information in the previous sentences. Instead, this description forms a comparison with the description of tropical forests in the previous sentence.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"6a5939c2","external_id":"d72a5a0b-bdd4-477d-a9f4-008853b581b1","vaultid":null,"uId":"303a58a6-0607-46f1-8e3c-48fabe36012b","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Paleontologists once thought that early apes lived in tropical forests, but recent research suggests that they may have actually lived in savannas. Tropical forests are humid and have many trees spaced close together. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> savannas are drier, and their trees are spaced further apart.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"1c278495-fe98-443e-a712-9481cc94754f","content":"<p>For instance,</p>"},{"id":"605c1f47-0ed2-491b-8c60-5b722b237271","content":"<p>In comparison,</p>"},{"id":"31ab7665-d5ca-44f9-a0fc-4e64eb3489e7","content":"<p>Firstly,</p>"},{"id":"3c981bbf-3c52-4d2e-add6-3e38a3bdb723","content":"<p>In conclusion,</p>"}],"keys":["605c1f47-0ed2-491b-8c60-5b722b237271"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. \"In comparison\" logically signals that the description of savannas in this sentence&mdash;that they are drier and their trees are spaced further apart&mdash;forms a comparison with the description of tropical forests in the previous sentence.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because \"for instance\" illogically signals that the description of savannas in this sentence exemplifies the description of tropical forests in the previous sentence. Instead, this description forms a comparison with the description of tropical forests. Choice C is incorrect because \"firstly\" illogically signals that the description of savannas in this sentence indicates the first in a series of things. Instead, this description forms a comparison with the description of tropical forests in the previous sentence. Choice D is incorrect because \"in conclusion\" illogically signals that the description of savannas in this sentence concludes or summarizes information in the previous sentences. Instead, this description forms a comparison with the description of tropical forests in the previous sentence.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323044,"updateDate":1730147323044}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323044, 1730147323044),
    ($SATQ$6b5bc97d$SATQ$, $SATQ$26c336bf-d732-4c21-a3f8-2979fdaf1d34$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$dc9b137d-8971-45ee-a8a3-eaf2becd4fcd$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>The Sasanian Empire lasted about 400 years (AD 224 to AD 651).</li>
<li>The Sasanians controlled an area spanning 1.4 million square miles.</li>
<li>This area included present-day Iran and Iraq.</li>
<li>The empire&rsquo;s capital was the ancient city of Ctesiphon.</li>
<li>Ctesiphon was located near present-day Baghdad, Iraq.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to specify the location of Ctesiphon. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"08b7cbb6-9ed8-4fc4-b0e4-34f26cd852f8","content":"<p>The Sasanian Empire began in AD 224 and ended in AD 651.</p>"},{"id":"bfd33f5a-261e-442c-9e38-578d430ff3af","content":"<p>The capital of the Sasanian Empire, which spanned 1.4 million square miles, was Ctesiphon.</p>"},{"id":"47744551-f990-47a6-8f76-2fb9515786ef","content":"<p>The Sasanians controlled an area of 1.4 million square miles, including present-day Iran and Iraq.</p>"},{"id":"59a6abce-3b9f-44e7-b4f2-3d286d345969","content":"<p>Ctesiphon, the capital of the Sasanian Empire, was located near present-day Baghdad, Iraq.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["59a6abce-3b9f-44e7-b4f2-3d286d345969"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. The sentence specifies the location of Ctesiphon, noting that it was located near present-day Baghdad, Iraq. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the sentence explains when the Sasanian Empire began and ended; it doesn&rsquo;t specify the location of Ctesiphon. Choice B is incorrect because the sentence emphasizes that Ctesiphon was the capital of the Sasanian Empire; it doesn&rsquo;t specify Ctesiphon&rsquo;s location. Choice C is incorrect because it emphasizes the size of the Sasanian Empire; it doesn&rsquo;t specify the location of Ctesiphon. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-014-SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$740a182c-2476-42c0-b66e-3997b40a2dc3$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"6b5bc97d","external_id":"26c336bf-d732-4c21-a3f8-2979fdaf1d34","vaultid":"dc9b137d-8971-45ee-a8a3-eaf2becd4fcd","uId":"801c9fc7-ee07-4439-bfda-0b27a409f430","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The Sasanian Empire lasted about 400 years (AD 224 to AD 651).</li>\n<li>The Sasanians controlled an area spanning 1.4 million square miles.</li>\n<li>This area included present-day Iran and Iraq.</li>\n<li>The empire&rsquo;s capital was the ancient city of Ctesiphon.</li>\n<li>Ctesiphon was located near present-day Baghdad, Iraq.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to specify the location of Ctesiphon. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"08b7cbb6-9ed8-4fc4-b0e4-34f26cd852f8","content":"<p>The Sasanian Empire began in AD 224 and ended in AD 651.</p>"},{"id":"bfd33f5a-261e-442c-9e38-578d430ff3af","content":"<p>The capital of the Sasanian Empire, which spanned 1.4 million square miles, was Ctesiphon.</p>"},{"id":"47744551-f990-47a6-8f76-2fb9515786ef","content":"<p>The Sasanians controlled an area of 1.4 million square miles, including present-day Iran and Iraq.</p>"},{"id":"59a6abce-3b9f-44e7-b4f2-3d286d345969","content":"<p>Ctesiphon, the capital of the Sasanian Empire, was located near present-day Baghdad, Iraq.</p>"}],"keys":["59a6abce-3b9f-44e7-b4f2-3d286d345969"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. The sentence specifies the location of Ctesiphon, noting that it was located near present-day Baghdad, Iraq. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the sentence explains when the Sasanian Empire began and ended; it doesn&rsquo;t specify the location of Ctesiphon. Choice B is incorrect because the sentence emphasizes that Ctesiphon was the capital of the Sasanian Empire; it doesn&rsquo;t specify Ctesiphon&rsquo;s location. Choice C is incorrect because it emphasizes the size of the Sasanian Empire; it doesn&rsquo;t specify the location of Ctesiphon. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-014-SYN","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"740a182c-2476-42c0-b66e-3997b40a2dc3","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959315,"updateDate":1691007959315}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959315, 1691007959315),
    ($SATQ$6c9df5d1$SATQ$, $SATQ$b8c0c1ce-add8-408a-9141-872682135f03$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$9cae7183-74aa-478b-9af0-9fede07f703b$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Some powerful works of literature have so influenced readers that new legislation has been passed as a result.</li>
<li><em>The Interesting Narrative</em> <em>of the Life of Olaudah Equiano</em> (1789) is the autobiography of a man who endured slavery on both sides of the Atlantic.</li>
<li>Equiano&rsquo;s book contributed to the passage of the Slave Trade Act of 1807.</li>
<li><em>The Jungle</em> (1906) is a fictional work by Upton Sinclair that describes unsanitary conditions in US meatpacking plants.</li>
<li>Sinclair&rsquo;s book contributed to the passage of the Pure Food and Drug Act in 1906.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to emphasize a difference between the two books. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"3a93d939-6f37-4b05-a00f-13f79ec4ea9d","content":"<p>Although both are powerful works of literature that contributed to new legislation, Equiano&rsquo;s book is an autobiography, while Sinclair&rsquo;s is fictional.</p>"},{"id":"13a9a55d-21e7-4980-89bd-a047acb1f089","content":"<p>They may have written about different topics, but Equiano and Sinclair both influenced readers.</p>"},{"id":"f4d3c1f9-6fd8-4f32-bcdc-93dd43c040ac","content":"<p>The 1807 Slave Trade Act resulted in part from a book by Equiano, while the 1906 Pure Food and Drug Act resulted in part from a book by Sinclair.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"df9a8b2f-13f2-4ba3-8881-d6cd11fb76f8","content":"<p><em>The Interesting Narrative of the Life of Olaudah Equiano</em> and <em>The Jungle</em> are two works of literature that contributed to new legislation (concerning the slave trade and food safety, respectively).&nbsp;</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["3a93d939-6f37-4b05-a00f-13f79ec4ea9d"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. This choice emphasizes a difference between the two books by using relevant information from the notes to contrast their genres.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This choice mentions a difference between the books (their different topics), but it emphasizes a similarity between the books (their influence on readers). Choice C is incorrect. This choice provides information about the books that reflects both a similarity (both resulted in new laws) and a difference (the specific laws that resulted), without emphasizing either. Choice D is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a difference between the two books. Instead, it <em>emphasizes a similarity</em>. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-SYN-H007$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$b75d6fb4-78a8-404f-92dd-9c8cff2fd6b3$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"6c9df5d1","external_id":"b8c0c1ce-add8-408a-9141-872682135f03","vaultid":"9cae7183-74aa-478b-9af0-9fede07f703b","uId":"195ff682-b0a1-46b1-a140-aa70b342b321","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Some powerful works of literature have so influenced readers that new legislation has been passed as a result.</li>\n<li><em>The Interesting Narrative</em> <em>of the Life of Olaudah Equiano</em> (1789) is the autobiography of a man who endured slavery on both sides of the Atlantic.</li>\n<li>Equiano&rsquo;s book contributed to the passage of the Slave Trade Act of 1807.</li>\n<li><em>The Jungle</em> (1906) is a fictional work by Upton Sinclair that describes unsanitary conditions in US meatpacking plants.</li>\n<li>Sinclair&rsquo;s book contributed to the passage of the Pure Food and Drug Act in 1906.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to emphasize a difference between the two books. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"3a93d939-6f37-4b05-a00f-13f79ec4ea9d","content":"<p>Although both are powerful works of literature that contributed to new legislation, Equiano&rsquo;s book is an autobiography, while Sinclair&rsquo;s is fictional.</p>"},{"id":"13a9a55d-21e7-4980-89bd-a047acb1f089","content":"<p>They may have written about different topics, but Equiano and Sinclair both influenced readers.</p>"},{"id":"f4d3c1f9-6fd8-4f32-bcdc-93dd43c040ac","content":"<p>The 1807 Slave Trade Act resulted in part from a book by Equiano, while the 1906 Pure Food and Drug Act resulted in part from a book by Sinclair.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"df9a8b2f-13f2-4ba3-8881-d6cd11fb76f8","content":"<p><em>The Interesting Narrative of the Life of Olaudah Equiano</em> and <em>The Jungle</em> are two works of literature that contributed to new legislation (concerning the slave trade and food safety, respectively).&nbsp;</p>"}],"keys":["3a93d939-6f37-4b05-a00f-13f79ec4ea9d"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. This choice emphasizes a difference between the two books by using relevant information from the notes to contrast their genres.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This choice mentions a difference between the books (their different topics), but it emphasizes a similarity between the books (their influence on readers). Choice C is incorrect. This choice provides information about the books that reflects both a similarity (both resulted in new laws) and a difference (the specific laws that resulted), without emphasizing either. Choice D is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a difference between the two books. Instead, it <em>emphasizes a similarity</em>. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-SYN-H007","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"b75d6fb4-78a8-404f-92dd-9c8cff2fd6b3","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959372,"updateDate":1691007959372}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959372, 1691007959372),
    ($SATQ$6d883838$SATQ$, $SATQ$8df570ab-4f44-46bf-b090-224ff81fa286$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>According to Duverger&rsquo;s law, countries with single-ballot majoritarian elections for single-member districts tend to polarize into two-party systems, wherein dueling political parties consistently dominate the political system. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> countries with proportional-representation electoral systems tend to support multi-partyism, under which power gets distributed among many political parties.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"ea1b340f-a192-4ddd-9352-78ba2f479306","content":"<p>Subsequently,</p>"},{"id":"ab1951a3-3325-41fd-9dc3-7b4a3c3b5b4d","content":"<p>Conversely,</p>"},{"id":"804c27af-2b39-4fd6-89d2-a9096882ad7c","content":"<p>For instance,</p>"},{"id":"19e7244f-3e63-44f7-8765-e1162735f60c","content":"<p>In other words,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["ab1951a3-3325-41fd-9dc3-7b4a3c3b5b4d"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. "Conversely" logically signals that the information in this sentence&mdash;that countries with proportional-representation electoral systems tend toward multi-partyism&mdash;contrasts with the previous information about countries with single-ballot majoritarian elections, which tend to have two-party systems.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because "subsequently" illogically signals that the information in this sentence about countries with proportional-representation electoral systems occurs later in a chronological sequence of events than the information in the previous sentence. Instead, it contrasts with the previous information. Choice C is incorrect because "for instance" illogically signals that the information in this sentence about countries with proportional-representation electoral systems is an example supporting the previous statement about countries with single-ballot majoritarian elections. Instead, it contrasts with the previous statement. Choice D is incorrect because "in other words" illogically signals that the information in this sentence about countries with proportional-representation electoral systems is a paraphrase or restatement of the previous information about countries with single-ballot majoritarian elections. Instead, it contrasts with the previous information.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"6d883838","external_id":"8df570ab-4f44-46bf-b090-224ff81fa286","vaultid":null,"uId":"9e6d8774-1a02-4da6-aadf-4bb84a1fc530","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>According to Duverger&rsquo;s law, countries with single-ballot majoritarian elections for single-member districts tend to polarize into two-party systems, wherein dueling political parties consistently dominate the political system. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> countries with proportional-representation electoral systems tend to support multi-partyism, under which power gets distributed among many political parties.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"ea1b340f-a192-4ddd-9352-78ba2f479306","content":"<p>Subsequently,</p>"},{"id":"ab1951a3-3325-41fd-9dc3-7b4a3c3b5b4d","content":"<p>Conversely,</p>"},{"id":"804c27af-2b39-4fd6-89d2-a9096882ad7c","content":"<p>For instance,</p>"},{"id":"19e7244f-3e63-44f7-8765-e1162735f60c","content":"<p>In other words,</p>"}],"keys":["ab1951a3-3325-41fd-9dc3-7b4a3c3b5b4d"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. \"Conversely\" logically signals that the information in this sentence&mdash;that countries with proportional-representation electoral systems tend toward multi-partyism&mdash;contrasts with the previous information about countries with single-ballot majoritarian elections, which tend to have two-party systems.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because \"subsequently\" illogically signals that the information in this sentence about countries with proportional-representation electoral systems occurs later in a chronological sequence of events than the information in the previous sentence. Instead, it contrasts with the previous information. Choice C is incorrect because \"for instance\" illogically signals that the information in this sentence about countries with proportional-representation electoral systems is an example supporting the previous statement about countries with single-ballot majoritarian elections. Instead, it contrasts with the previous statement. Choice D is incorrect because \"in other words\" illogically signals that the information in this sentence about countries with proportional-representation electoral systems is a paraphrase or restatement of the previous information about countries with single-ballot majoritarian elections. Instead, it contrasts with the previous information.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323043,"updateDate":1730147323043}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323043, 1730147323043),
    ($SATQ$6de02dfa$SATQ$, $SATQ$e49c3a3d-316e-4d89-a024-eb5e003eb43b$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:​</p>
<ul>
<li>Thailand&rsquo;s annual Songkran Water Festival is held each April.</li>
<li>It marks Songkran, the traditional Thai New Year.</li>
<li>People splash and spray each other for fun at the festival&rsquo;s community-wide water fights.</li>
<li>In Bangkok, thousands gather along Silom Road for the city&rsquo;s largest water fight.</li>
<li>In Chiang Mai, thousands gather at a historical monument called the Tha Phae Gate for the city&rsquo;s largest water fight.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to emphasize a similarity in how people in Bangkok and Chiang Mai celebrate Songkran. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"4c86506d-b5ec-4fa0-954f-4115f14a4465","content":"<p>The largest water fight in Bangkok takes place along a city street, whereas the largest water fight in Chiang Mai takes place at a historical monument.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"8165ad76-7fc0-4796-a50a-2b9e42c87c10","content":"<p>In both Bangkok and Chiang Mai, thousands gather to celebrate Songkran with water fights.</p>"},{"id":"777134f8-8319-4927-856d-f9552b2ffdbe","content":"<p>People in both Bangkok and Chiang Mai celebrate Songkran, but they don&rsquo;t do so in exactly the same way.</p>"},{"id":"38e6ad1b-c76a-4a45-b96b-111b03927fd2","content":"<p>Each April, people in Thailand celebrate Songkran, the traditional Thai New Year.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["8165ad76-7fc0-4796-a50a-2b9e42c87c10"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes a similarity in how people in Bangkok and Chiang Mai celebrate Songkran, indicating that people in both cities gather to celebrate with water fights.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence notes the different locations of the largest water fight in Bangkok and the largest water fight in Chiang Mai; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity in how people in Bangkok and Chiang Mai celebrate Songkran. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence indicates that people in Bangkok and Chiang Mai don&rsquo;t celebrate Songkran in exactly the same way; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity in how people in the two cities celebrate Songkran. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence explains when people in Thailand celebrate Songkran; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity in how people in Bangkok and Chiang Mai celebrate Songkran.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"6de02dfa","external_id":"e49c3a3d-316e-4d89-a024-eb5e003eb43b","vaultid":null,"uId":"606c3ecf-8365-4221-b6a3-059c5ba79ffe","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:​</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Thailand&rsquo;s annual Songkran Water Festival is held each April.</li>\n<li>It marks Songkran, the traditional Thai New Year.</li>\n<li>People splash and spray each other for fun at the festival&rsquo;s community-wide water fights.</li>\n<li>In Bangkok, thousands gather along Silom Road for the city&rsquo;s largest water fight.</li>\n<li>In Chiang Mai, thousands gather at a historical monument called the Tha Phae Gate for the city&rsquo;s largest water fight.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to emphasize a similarity in how people in Bangkok and Chiang Mai celebrate Songkran. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"4c86506d-b5ec-4fa0-954f-4115f14a4465","content":"<p>The largest water fight in Bangkok takes place along a city street, whereas the largest water fight in Chiang Mai takes place at a historical monument.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"8165ad76-7fc0-4796-a50a-2b9e42c87c10","content":"<p>In both Bangkok and Chiang Mai, thousands gather to celebrate Songkran with water fights.</p>"},{"id":"777134f8-8319-4927-856d-f9552b2ffdbe","content":"<p>People in both Bangkok and Chiang Mai celebrate Songkran, but they don&rsquo;t do so in exactly the same way.</p>"},{"id":"38e6ad1b-c76a-4a45-b96b-111b03927fd2","content":"<p>Each April, people in Thailand celebrate Songkran, the traditional Thai New Year.</p>"}],"keys":["8165ad76-7fc0-4796-a50a-2b9e42c87c10"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes a similarity in how people in Bangkok and Chiang Mai celebrate Songkran, indicating that people in both cities gather to celebrate with water fights.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence notes the different locations of the largest water fight in Bangkok and the largest water fight in Chiang Mai; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity in how people in Bangkok and Chiang Mai celebrate Songkran. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence indicates that people in Bangkok and Chiang Mai don&rsquo;t celebrate Songkran in exactly the same way; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity in how people in the two cities celebrate Songkran. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence explains when people in Thailand celebrate Songkran; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity in how people in Bangkok and Chiang Mai celebrate Songkran.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323034,"updateDate":1730147323034}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323034, 1730147323034),
    ($SATQ$6e0c60da$SATQ$, $SATQ$54d57f5e-7d9a-4185-9a93-a5c476e4564a$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$c520996d-a385-4651-b88b-ed0fa16a52c8$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>When one looks at the dark craggy vistas in Hitoshi Fugo&rsquo;s evocative photo series, one&rsquo;s mind might wander off to the cratered surfaces of faraway planets. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> it&rsquo;s the series&rsquo; title, <em>Flying Frying Pan</em>, that brings one back to Earth, reminding the viewer that each photo is actually a close-up view of a familiar household object: a frying pan.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"1f97945d-98bd-45c5-9ab1-10ec8b50ac19","content":"<p>Consequently,</p>"},{"id":"32dc3903-d9e0-4eb9-917b-cf89dd4f5c3f","content":"<p>Alternatively,</p>"},{"id":"c7c0cfb6-7c11-4f7b-89c8-07c0e3b8e7ce","content":"<p>Ultimately,</p>"},{"id":"467bc548-1c5b-48a2-9ace-e06990f113c3","content":"<p>Additionally,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["c7c0cfb6-7c11-4f7b-89c8-07c0e3b8e7ce"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer. The first sentence describes an experience that the viewer has when they&rsquo;re looking at the photos: they imagine other planets. This sentence describes an experience that the viewer has afterward: the title reminds them that the photos are of frying pans, bringing them back to reality. &ldquo;Ultimately&rdquo; is a transition that means &ldquo;eventually&rdquo; or &ldquo;in the end,&rdquo; so it fits the context perfectly. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This choice uses a cause-and-effect transition, which doesn&rsquo;t make sense here. The viewer imagining other planets when they&rsquo;re looking at the photos doesn&rsquo;t cause the title to bring them back to reality. Choice B is incorrect. This choice uses a transition that indicates another option or possibility, which doesn&rsquo;t make sense here. Rather, the viewer has both experiences: first the viewer imagines that they&rsquo;re looking at another planet, and then the title reminds them that it&rsquo;s just a frying pan. Choice D is incorrect. This choice uses a transition that indicates the addition of an agreeing idea. But the viewer&rsquo;s experience in the second sentence is actually the opposite of the viewer&rsquo;s experience in the first sentence. In the first sentence, the viewer is imagining that they&rsquo;re seeing a landscape from another planet. In the second sentence, the viewer is reminded that they&rsquo;re looking at a frying pan. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-TRA-H002$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$fea9339a-de25-4093-8c58-72870dac306c$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"6e0c60da","external_id":"54d57f5e-7d9a-4185-9a93-a5c476e4564a","vaultid":"c520996d-a385-4651-b88b-ed0fa16a52c8","uId":"46ffe705-9908-43fc-a9a8-9b173c6a3e62","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>When one looks at the dark craggy vistas in Hitoshi Fugo&rsquo;s evocative photo series, one&rsquo;s mind might wander off to the cratered surfaces of faraway planets. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> it&rsquo;s the series&rsquo; title, <em>Flying Frying Pan</em>, that brings one back to Earth, reminding the viewer that each photo is actually a close-up view of a familiar household object: a frying pan.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"1f97945d-98bd-45c5-9ab1-10ec8b50ac19","content":"<p>Consequently,</p>"},{"id":"32dc3903-d9e0-4eb9-917b-cf89dd4f5c3f","content":"<p>Alternatively,</p>"},{"id":"c7c0cfb6-7c11-4f7b-89c8-07c0e3b8e7ce","content":"<p>Ultimately,</p>"},{"id":"467bc548-1c5b-48a2-9ace-e06990f113c3","content":"<p>Additionally,</p>"}],"keys":["c7c0cfb6-7c11-4f7b-89c8-07c0e3b8e7ce"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer. The first sentence describes an experience that the viewer has when they&rsquo;re looking at the photos: they imagine other planets. This sentence describes an experience that the viewer has afterward: the title reminds them that the photos are of frying pans, bringing them back to reality. &ldquo;Ultimately&rdquo; is a transition that means &ldquo;eventually&rdquo; or &ldquo;in the end,&rdquo; so it fits the context perfectly. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This choice uses a cause-and-effect transition, which doesn&rsquo;t make sense here. The viewer imagining other planets when they&rsquo;re looking at the photos doesn&rsquo;t cause the title to bring them back to reality. Choice B is incorrect. This choice uses a transition that indicates another option or possibility, which doesn&rsquo;t make sense here. Rather, the viewer has both experiences: first the viewer imagines that they&rsquo;re looking at another planet, and then the title reminds them that it&rsquo;s just a frying pan. Choice D is incorrect. This choice uses a transition that indicates the addition of an agreeing idea. But the viewer&rsquo;s experience in the second sentence is actually the opposite of the viewer&rsquo;s experience in the first sentence. In the first sentence, the viewer is imagining that they&rsquo;re seeing a landscape from another planet. In the second sentence, the viewer is reminded that they&rsquo;re looking at a frying pan. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-TRA-H002","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"fea9339a-de25-4093-8c58-72870dac306c","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959373,"updateDate":1691007959373}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959373, 1691007959373),
    ($SATQ$70538b9a$SATQ$, $SATQ$4147c82e-66fa-4dc9-8b24-a4de406b8f81$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>In the 1930s, the Imperial Sugar Cane Institute in India sought to limit the country&rsquo;s dependence on imported sugarcane.</li>
<li>The institute enlisted botanist Janaki Ammal to breed a local variety of sugarcane.</li>
<li>She crossbred the imported sugarcane species <em>Saccharum officinarum </em>with grasses native to India.</li>
<li>She succeeded in creating sugarcane hybrids well suited to India&rsquo;s climate.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to emphasize Janaki Ammal&rsquo;s achievement. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"5e2a30d3-bd93-4224-871a-2f8181e56010","content":"<p>By crossbreeding the imported sugarcane species <em>Saccharum officinarum </em>with grasses native to India, Ammal succeeded in creating sugarcane hybrids well suited to India&rsquo;s climate.</p>"},{"id":"84bcdb8b-cf14-4d34-8465-ebc8b3e843fd","content":"<p>In the 1930s, the Imperial Sugar Cane Institute, which enlisted Ammal, sought to limit dependence on imported sugarcane.</p>"},{"id":"057c560d-292b-4b8a-8f59-b98120d4a24c","content":"<p>Ammal was enlisted by the Imperial Sugar Cane Institute at a time when a local variety of sugarcane needed to be produced.</p>"},{"id":"54fe1e27-7b70-44a5-ad45-8828e875e879","content":"<p>As part of efforts to breed a local variety of sugarcane, an imported sugarcane species called <em>Saccharum officinarum </em>was crossbred with grasses native to India.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["5e2a30d3-bd93-4224-871a-2f8181e56010"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes Janaki Ammal&rsquo;s achievement, explaining that she successfully created sugarcane hybrids that are well suited to India&rsquo;s climate by crossbreeding an imported sugarcane species with grasses native to India.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes the goal of the Imperial Sugar Cane Institute in the 1930s; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize Janaki Ammal&rsquo;s achievement. Choice C is incorrect. While the sentence mentions Ammal, it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize her achievement of successfully creating sugarcane hybrids. Choice D is incorrect. While the sentence mentions the achievement of crossbreeding imported sugarcane species with grasses native to India, it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize the achievement as belonging to Janaki Ammal.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"70538b9a","external_id":"4147c82e-66fa-4dc9-8b24-a4de406b8f81","vaultid":null,"uId":"eafc5647-2e0c-4b61-b534-44b7273e76bc","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>In the 1930s, the Imperial Sugar Cane Institute in India sought to limit the country&rsquo;s dependence on imported sugarcane.</li>\n<li>The institute enlisted botanist Janaki Ammal to breed a local variety of sugarcane.</li>\n<li>She crossbred the imported sugarcane species <em>Saccharum officinarum </em>with grasses native to India.</li>\n<li>She succeeded in creating sugarcane hybrids well suited to India&rsquo;s climate.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to emphasize Janaki Ammal&rsquo;s achievement. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"5e2a30d3-bd93-4224-871a-2f8181e56010","content":"<p>By crossbreeding the imported sugarcane species <em>Saccharum officinarum </em>with grasses native to India, Ammal succeeded in creating sugarcane hybrids well suited to India&rsquo;s climate.</p>"},{"id":"84bcdb8b-cf14-4d34-8465-ebc8b3e843fd","content":"<p>In the 1930s, the Imperial Sugar Cane Institute, which enlisted Ammal, sought to limit dependence on imported sugarcane.</p>"},{"id":"057c560d-292b-4b8a-8f59-b98120d4a24c","content":"<p>Ammal was enlisted by the Imperial Sugar Cane Institute at a time when a local variety of sugarcane needed to be produced.</p>"},{"id":"54fe1e27-7b70-44a5-ad45-8828e875e879","content":"<p>As part of efforts to breed a local variety of sugarcane, an imported sugarcane species called <em>Saccharum officinarum </em>was crossbred with grasses native to India.</p>"}],"keys":["5e2a30d3-bd93-4224-871a-2f8181e56010"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes Janaki Ammal&rsquo;s achievement, explaining that she successfully created sugarcane hybrids that are well suited to India&rsquo;s climate by crossbreeding an imported sugarcane species with grasses native to India.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes the goal of the Imperial Sugar Cane Institute in the 1930s; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize Janaki Ammal&rsquo;s achievement. Choice C is incorrect. While the sentence mentions Ammal, it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize her achievement of successfully creating sugarcane hybrids. Choice D is incorrect. While the sentence mentions the achievement of crossbreeding imported sugarcane species with grasses native to India, it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize the achievement as belonging to Janaki Ammal.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323048,"updateDate":1730147323048}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323048, 1730147323048),
    ($SATQ$7298633c$SATQ$, $SATQ$cc40f3a3-bd4f-4d88-bc2c-455e880ace70$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Grimanesa Amoros is a Peruvian American artist well known for her LED light sculptures.</li>
<li>Her sculpture <em>Uros Island</em> is made of smooth multicolored LED domes.</li>
<li>It occupies 335 cubic feet of space.</li>
<li>Her sculpture <em>Fortuna</em> is made of entangled blue and white LED tubes.</li>
<li>It occupies 19,950 cubic feet of space.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to emphasize a similarity between <em>Uros Island</em> and <em>Fortuna</em>. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"f10af62e-701b-4689-8824-b0476d9367b9","content":"<p>The smooth LED domes of Grimanesa Amoros&rsquo;s <em>Uros Island</em> stand in contrast to the tangled LED tubes of <em>Fortuna</em>.</p>"},{"id":"822c6d0a-b0b3-498e-ab61-53e78faf3cb0","content":"<p>At 19,950 cubic feet in size, Grimanesa Amoros&rsquo;s <em>Fortuna</em> cuts a larger figure than the 335-cubic-foot <em>Uros Island</em>.</p>"},{"id":"e60046de-f091-46d3-bdc9-2e5b84747f84","content":"<p>Grimanesa Amoros is the artist behind <em>Uros Island</em>&mdash;a sculpture made of smooth multicolored LED domes.</p>"},{"id":"cb6cac00-6fa7-4078-8da9-fb395a4e56fb","content":"<p><em>Uros Island</em> is an LED light sculpture made by Grimanesa Amoros, as is <em>Fortuna</em>.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["cb6cac00-6fa7-4078-8da9-fb395a4e56fb"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes a similarity between the sculptures, noting that both <em>Uros Island</em> and <em>Fortuna</em> are LED light sculptures created by Grimanesa Amoros.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. Noting that <em>Uros Island</em>&rsquo;s smooth LED domes contrast with <em>Fortuna</em>&rsquo;s tangled LED tubes, the sentence emphasizes a difference between the two sculptures rather than a similarity. Choice B is incorrect. Contrasting the respective sizes of <em>Uros Island</em> and <em>Fortuna</em>, the sentence emphasizes a difference between the two sculptures rather than a similarity. Choice C is incorrect. While the sentence describes <em>Uros Island</em>, it doesn&rsquo;t mention <em>Fortuna</em> or emphasize any similarity between the two sculptures.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7298633c","external_